{
	"_comment": "Single source of truth for remote LLM API providers and per-model pricing. Both drivers (AHK api_remote.ahk and HS api_remote.lua) load this file at boot — add a provider here first, then reload the driver. `format` is openai, anthropic, gemini, backboard (Backboard's assistant/thread API, key in X-API-Key, models written <llm_provider>/<model_name>) or decisions (TypeSafe's System One protocol: typed questions in, answers with probabilities out; base_url is the full endpoint and the key goes in Authorization: Bearer). A decisions provider serves Jev, which is not a chat model: it is offered only as the agent's System 1. The request shapes of backboard and decisions live in _shared/lua/llm/remote_formats.lua. `thinking_dialect` (optional) says how the provider carries each reasoning control kind of _shared/modules/llm/thinking_off.json: kind -> body fields deep-merged into the request (a field the body already sets wins), the string $level replaced by the model family's level. A kind the provider does not list is never sent (openai_compat lists none: it may point at a strict endpoint). Sources: platform.claude.com build-with-claude/thinking and effort, developers.openai.com guides/reasoning, ai.google.dev thinking, docs.x.ai reasoning, docs.mistral.ai reasoning, api-docs.deepseek.com thinking_mode, docs.cohere.com compatibility-api, inference-docs.cerebras.ai reasoning, openrouter.ai reasoning-tokens, console.groq.com reasoning, docs.together.ai reasoning-models-guide, docs.fireworks.ai post-chatcompletions (checked 2026-10-30). Every provider after fireworks names the official pages its address, key, listing, default model and dialect were read from in its _source (checked 2026-10-30).",
